---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | overtimechecker.com';
const description = 'How overtimechecker.com handles your data: what we collect, what we don\'t, cookies, advertising, our attorney case-review referral, and your rights under GDPR, CCPA, and COPPA.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Effective Date: May 14, 2026 &middot; Last Updated: July 2026.</em></p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy describes how overtimechecker.com ("we," "us," or "our"), operated by The Click Lab, collects, uses, and shares information when you visit our website at overtimechecker.com. We are committed to handling your data transparently, including when it is shared with attorneys through our case-review form. By using this site, you agree to the practices described below.</p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>Browsing the calculator and guides.</strong> Any data entered into the overtime calculator &mdash; your hourly rate, hours worked, state of employment, bonus or commission amounts &mdash; runs entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter to estimate overtime pay are not transmitted to our servers, are not stored server-side, and are not logged. Reading the calculator or any guide on this site, on its own, does not send us your personal information.</p>
  <p><strong>If you submit the case-review form.</strong> The homepage includes an optional "Get my free case review" form for Overtime Pay questions. If you fill it out and submit it, we collect your first and last name, email address, phone number, ZIP code, approximate incident date, your description of what happened, and the timestamp and exact text of the consent you agreed to. Section 5 below explains exactly what happens to this information.</p>
  <p><strong>If you email us.</strong> If you contact us via email, we receive the information you choose to send (your name, email address, and message content).</p>
  <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, we and our service providers automatically collect limited technical information when you visit, including IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating system, referring URL, pages visited, time spent on pages, and approximate geographic location derived from IP. This is used for analytics, performance, and security purposes.</p>
  <p><strong>Cookies and similar technologies.</strong> We use cookies and similar tracking technologies. See Section 4 below for details.</p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and improve the site and our overtime calculator</li>
    <li>To analyze usage trends and understand which guides and tools are most useful</li>
    <li>To respond to contact inquiries and corrections</li>
    <li>To route case-review form submissions to attorneys or their agents for evaluation and follow-up contact, as described in Section 5</li>
    <li>To serve relevant advertising through Google AdSense</li>
    <li>To detect and prevent fraud, abuse, or violations of our Terms of Service</li>
    <li>To comply with applicable legal obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>We use Google AdSense, a third-party advertising service provided by Google LLC, to display advertisements on this website. Google uses cookies &mdash; including the DoubleClick DART cookie &mdash; to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to our site and other sites on the internet.</p>
  <p>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</p>
  <p>You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google's Ads Settings at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.google.com/settings/ads</a>. You may also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.aboutads.info/choices</a> (for U.S. residents) or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.youronlinechoices.eu</a> (for EU residents).</p>
  <p>Google's privacy policy is available at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

  <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
  <p>A cookie is a small text file stored on your device by your browser. We use three categories of cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> required for basic site functionality, such as remembering your cookie consent preferences.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> (Google Analytics, where installed) used to understand aggregate site usage &mdash; which pages are popular, where visitors come from, and how the site performs.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising cookies</strong> (via Google AdSense and its partners) used to serve relevant ads and to measure ad performance.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can control cookies through your browser settings, including blocking or deleting them, although disabling cookies may affect site functionality. By continuing to use this site, you consent to our use of cookies as described in this policy. EU/UK/EEA users will be shown a cookie consent banner where required by law.</p>

  <h2>5. Sharing Your Information</h2>
  <p>If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it. The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates overtimechecker.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals.</p>
  <p>By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email &mdash; including by automated dialing technology &mdash; by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.</p>
  <p>Outside of the case-review form, we do not sell personal information for money. We share limited information only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> (hosting, analytics, ad networks) who process data on our behalf under confidentiality obligations. Current service providers include Google AdSense, Google Analytics, Cloudflare (DNS, edge delivery, and lead-intake processing), and Hostinger (registrar).</li>
    <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> when required by law, subpoena, or court order.</li>
    <li><strong>Successors</strong> in the event of a business transfer, merger, or acquisition.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Opting Out of the Case-Review Form</h2>
  <p>The simplest opt-out is not to submit the case-review form &mdash; browsing the calculator and guides never sends us your personal information, and nothing about using the rest of the site requires you to use the form.</p>
  <p>If you've already submitted the form and want to withdraw consent or have your information deleted from our records or an attorney's, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <strong>[OPT-OUT]</strong>, or</li>
    <li>Visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://theclicklab.agency/optout</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We will process opt-out requests promptly and pass the request along to any attorney or agent who received your information where required.</p>

  <h2>7. Your Rights Under GDPR (EU/UK/EEA Users)</h2>
  <p>If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you have the following rights under the General Data Protection Regulation: the right to access, correct, erase ("right to be forgotten"), restrict processing of, port, and object to processing of your personal data. You also have the right to withdraw consent at any time and to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p>
  <p>Our lawful bases for processing are (a) your consent (for advertising and analytics cookies, and separately for submitting the case-review form and being contacted about it &mdash; withdrawable at any time via Section 6 above), and (b) our legitimate interest in operating and securing the site. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>8. Your Rights Under CCPA (California Residents)</h2>
  <p>If you are a California resident, you have the following rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The right to know what personal information we collect and how it is used.</li>
    <li>The right to request deletion of personal information.</li>
    <li>The right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information.</li>
    <li>The right to non-discrimination for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Sharing your case-review submission with attorneys in exchange for compensation, as described in Section 5, may be considered a "sale" or "sharing" of personal information under the CCPA/CPRA. Using advertising cookies may also be considered "sharing." Anonymous browsing of the calculator and guides is never sold or shared &mdash; only information you affirmatively submit through the case-review form. To opt out of the sale or sharing of your information, use the channels in Section 6 above, use your browser's Global Privacy Control signal for advertising cookies, or email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line "CCPA Opt-Out Request." We will respond within 45 days.</p>

  <h2>9. Children's Privacy (COPPA)</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13, and the case-review form requires the submitter to confirm they are 18 or older. If we learn that we have collected such information, we will delete it promptly. Parents or guardians who believe their child has submitted information should contact <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <h2>10. Data Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect information, including HTTPS for all traffic and access controls on internal systems. However, no system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>11. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>We retain contact-form submissions and case-review form submissions for no longer than 24 months unless a longer period is required by law. Server access logs are retained for up to 90 days. Aggregated analytics data may be retained for up to 26 months in accordance with Google Analytics defaults.</p>

  <h2>12. International Data Transfers</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on servers that may be located outside your country of residence. By using this site, you consent to the transfer of your information to such jurisdictions. We rely on Standard Contractual Clauses or equivalent safeguards for transfers of EU/UK personal data to jurisdictions without an adequacy decision.</p>

  <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be announced by updating the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page and, when significant, by displaying a banner on the homepage for at least 30 days. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

  <h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>For any privacy-related questions, requests, or complaints, contact:</p>
  <p>The Click Lab<br />Email: <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
